WEBVTT

00:00.720 --> 00:01.680
Mark 7

00:01.680 --> 00:07.560
Now when the Pharisees gathered to him with some of the scribes who had come from Jerusalem,

00:08.180 --> 00:12.940
they saw that some of his disciples ate with hands that were defiled, that is, unwashed.

00:13.380 --> 00:17.540
For the Pharisees and all the Jews do not eat unless they wash their hands,

00:17.700 --> 00:19.420
holding to the tradition of the elders.

00:20.120 --> 00:23.860
And when they come from the marketplace, they do not eat unless they wash.

00:24.380 --> 00:27.020
And there are many other traditions that they observe,

00:27.020 --> 00:31.600
such as the washing of cups and pots, and copper vessels and dining couches.

00:31.920 --> 00:34.340
And the Pharisees and the scribes asked him,

00:35.080 --> 00:38.880
Why do your disciples not walk according to the tradition of the elders,

00:39.100 --> 00:41.660
but eat with defiled hands?

00:42.520 --> 00:43.640
And he said to them,

00:44.460 --> 00:47.160
Well did Isaiah prophesy of you hypocrites.

00:47.480 --> 00:52.660
As it is written, this people honors me with their lips, but their heart is far from me.

00:52.780 --> 00:54.940
In vain do they worship me,

00:55.280 --> 00:57.000
teaching as doctrines the commandments,

00:57.020 --> 01:02.240
You leave the commandment of God and hold to the tradition of men.

01:03.040 --> 01:03.940
And he said to them,

01:04.700 --> 01:10.260
You have a fine way of rejecting the commandment of God in order to establish your tradition.

01:11.100 --> 01:12.040
For Moses said,

01:12.480 --> 01:19.320
But you say,

01:19.880 --> 01:22.000
If a man tells his father or his mother,

01:22.500 --> 01:26.380
Whatever you would have gained from me is Corban, that is, given to God,

01:26.380 --> 01:26.580
then I will give you the commandment of God.

01:26.580 --> 01:26.600
And he said to them,

01:26.600 --> 01:27.000
You have a fine way of rejecting the commandment of God in order to establish your tradition.

01:27.020 --> 01:30.360
Then you no longer permit him to do anything for his father or mother,

01:30.920 --> 01:34.920
thus making void the word of God by your tradition that you have handed down,

01:35.260 --> 01:37.000
and many such things you do.

01:37.720 --> 01:40.420
And he called the people to him again and said to them,

01:41.100 --> 01:43.520
Hear me, all of you, and understand.

01:44.140 --> 01:48.000
There is nothing outside a person that by going into him can defile him.

01:48.380 --> 01:51.700
But the things that come out of a person are what defile him.

01:52.380 --> 01:54.880
And when he had entered the house and left the people,

01:54.880 --> 01:57.000
his disciples asked him about the people,

01:57.000 --> 01:58.760
and he said to them,

01:59.480 --> 02:01.640
Then are you also without understanding?

02:02.780 --> 02:07.140
Do you not see that whatever goes into a person from outside cannot defile him,

02:07.700 --> 02:11.340
since it enters not his heart, but his stomach, and is expelled?

02:12.140 --> 02:15.280
Thus he declared all foods clean, and he said,

02:15.980 --> 02:18.800
What comes out of a person is what defiles him.

02:19.340 --> 02:21.920
For from within, out of the heart of man,

02:21.920 --> 02:26.560
come evil thoughts, sexual immorality, theft, murder, adultery,

02:26.560 --> 02:32.980
coveting, wickedness, deceit, sensuality, envy, slander, pride, foolishness.

02:33.420 --> 02:37.980
All these evil things come from within, and they defile a person.

02:39.740 --> 02:44.040
And from there he arose and went away to the region of Tyre and Sidon.

02:44.740 --> 02:48.740
And he entered a house and did not want anyone to know, yet he could not be hidden.

02:49.460 --> 02:53.500
But immediately a woman whose little daughter had an unclean spirit heard of him

02:53.500 --> 02:55.640
and came and fell down at his feet.

02:56.560 --> 02:59.640
Now the woman was a Gentile, a Syrophoenician by birth.

03:00.380 --> 03:03.080
And she begged him to cast the demon out of her daughter.

03:03.640 --> 03:04.500
And he said to her,

03:05.280 --> 03:06.980
Let the children be fed first,

03:07.420 --> 03:11.080
for it is not right to take the children's bread and throw it to the dogs.

03:11.780 --> 03:13.320
But she answered him,

03:14.000 --> 03:19.740
Yes, Lord, yet even the dogs under the table eat the children's crumbs.

03:20.380 --> 03:21.860
And he said to her,

03:22.740 --> 03:24.940
For this statement you may go your way.

03:25.520 --> 03:26.540
The demon has left you.

03:27.420 --> 03:31.720
And she went home and found the child lying in bed and the demon gone.

03:32.920 --> 03:37.360
Then he returned from the region of Tyre and went through Sidon to the Sea of Galilee

03:37.360 --> 03:39.000
in the region of the Decapolis.

03:39.900 --> 03:43.440
And they brought to him a man who was deaf and had a speech impediment,

03:43.780 --> 03:46.080
and they begged him to lay his hand on him.

03:46.860 --> 03:49.080
And taking him aside from the crowd privately,

03:49.440 --> 03:53.340
he put his fingers into his ears and after spitting touched his tongue.

03:53.620 --> 03:56.340
And looking up to heaven he sighed and said to him,

03:56.540 --> 03:56.780
And he said to him,

03:57.660 --> 04:00.100
Ephatha,

04:00.940 --> 04:01.640
that is,

04:02.380 --> 04:04.520
be opened.

04:05.400 --> 04:09.480
And his ears were opened, his tongue was released, and he spoke plainly.

04:09.980 --> 04:12.420
And Jesus charged them to tell no one.

04:12.780 --> 04:15.980
But the more he charged them, the more zealously they proclaimed it.

04:16.300 --> 04:18.680
And they were astonished beyond measure, saying,

04:19.400 --> 04:21.060
He has done all things well.

04:21.160 --> 04:23.780
He even makes the deaf hear and the mute speak.

